#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0256 expect=violation domain=ADAE
#note "MECHANISM PIN - Q17-a absent-domain EmptyResult. NO ADSL block at all. distinct over the unresolvable ADSL answers the SET codomain's EmptyResult - the EMPTY set - so `USUBJID not in $adsl_usubjid` fires on BOTH populated rows. Loud-by-design when ADSL is missing (every ADaM subject is then untraceable), matching the sheet's intent."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
#expectViolationCount 2
#expectViolationAt row=1 USUBJID=01-701-1015
#expectViolationAt row=2 USUBJID=01-701-1023
dataset ADAE
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col AEDECOD type=Char
---
S1 | 01-701-1015 | HEADACHE
